                <divLine xml:id="m-5c08ee37-67e7-4c3a-bf96-aaae34e2eed6" facs="#m-6383f6c6-b4bc-4a39-b6ad-2a19a920dbd5" form="finalis" />
              </layer>
            </staff>
            <div xml:id="m-ebf04255-90c9-4821-8789-ba1c64960ca2">
              <lg xml:id="m-0705463c-01f8-4671-8432-c451f6f6dc44">
                <l xml:id="m-8465854c-ce6a-44b0-9104-83ae6acbe319" facs="#m-b95cda05-a06d-416c-9f30-735aeee8a8d1" label="ambiguous">Good Friday</l><l xml:id="m-1f806722-1279-459c-8b8e-ff09eb0ce43b" facs="#m-7ef56ee2-0585-4e54-baeb-5bda8fd6b081" label="ambiguous">736</l><l xml:id="m-e9098931-f0a8-4161-84f6-e78f8b13673d" facs="#m-df8a258c-86a2-4cc8-a904-b711674b07d0" label="ambiguous">dit.</l><l xml:id="m-ef17e7ff-9b2d-47b8-9666-448a57dfba4d" facs="#m-7406b934-02ac-43bf-b75d-9b03a817b93c" label="ambiguous">di</l><l xml:id="m-e664a018-8f40-468d-96d5-184036446210" facs="#m-44c964db-2993-453d-b40b-53af18d9d244" label="lyrics-like">pe-pén¬</l><l xml:id="m-50ba26d4-0d84-445d-a294-5be4329d3773" facs="#m-375064c1-cfc4-4d90-8307-ce04487d5a4f" label="lyrics-like">Al : K. Ve-ní-te,</l><l xml:id="m-5664a212-aada-453b-ab48-a1ccb6476b4b" facs="#m-fbb623b4-2de8-417f-a99c-eafdfb749063" label="lyrics-like">ad-oré- mus.</l><l xml:id="m-23f281a4-b7ab-4259-b279-9a937816c606" facs="#m-fb145439-3d3b-4f3e-b82f-f00da33629c6" label="text-like">After the antiphon, all, except the celebrant vith the Cross and the candle</l><l xml:id="m-873138c9-e74d-4b25-9012-aa093a6b8375" facs="#m-9b747a39-049d-4e0c-854e-afb261b4acb6" label="text-like">bearers, hneel and adore in silence for a fewo moments.</l><l xml:id="m-7220fcff-39a8-4642-9923-31f6361bd2ff" facs="#m-df25ee67-7ef2-45a8-b8a4-11394833e0f6" label="text-like">The celebrant then soes to the middle of the altar and uncovers the Cross</l><l xml:id="m-187b7322-a64d-415f-84e4-bf7e12257bb8" facs="#m-1cae766b-6720-4f99-bcd1-0bc13c836936" label="text-like">completely. He raises it, and in a higher hey sines again Ecce lignum</l><l xml:id="m-853d294c-1704-4ef8-86bd-cef26ebb0bb0" facs="#m-38edb22e-904b-4d0b-940d-5499a42434a7" label="lyrics-like">Crúcis. The others join in the singing and kneel dowomn, as before.</l><l xml:id="m-11938c27-ad22-47b7-9548-58b4b219e7cd" facs="#m-0dc3a459-d2ae-4cb5-a3d8-73eed703c341" label="text-like">The celebrant then goes to the middle of the altar and uncovers the Cross</l><l xml:id="m-515ec452-de41-4525-ab69-5ab54b7af0bf" facs="#m-6a2991d4-26bd-4cdd-9a33-4fc3eff98b63" label="text-like">completely; he then raises it, and in a still higher hey sings again Ecce lignum</l><l xml:id="m-c3dd18c6-0be2-4307-a375-ff563a81ef5b" facs="#m-c5908b59-35ba-43e2-9474-53c7535e9e68" label="lyrics-like">Crúcis. The others then join in the singing and kneel dowm, as before.</l><l xml:id="m-ab3aabcf-07ff-4232-991f-6c23c6dc529b" facs="#m-038b109e-39c5-4a75-ad50-6032edfc7f4f" label="text-like">17. After its unveiling the solemn adoration of the Cross tahes place in this</l><l xml:id="m-53321507-b84a-4e42-b828-94f945de6e76" facs="#m-b7347a57-c527-48ea-97d0-bed0b1c3485f" label="text-like">vay: the unveiled Cross is given by the celebrant to two acolytes lor serversl</l><l xml:id="m-879b4e68-f572-4ac1-9e11-2276fb82ea12" facs="#m-dab18208-1643-4bf2-bcf8-34b6bd6ecc31" label="text-like">vho stand on the predella in the middle of the altar facing ine people; they</l><l xml:id="m-49bbad01-b83c-49e0-8c8e-b6d66646d087" facs="#m-4c3ff012-f27c-4483-a15e-e3aa724b31a3" label="text-like">hold it on each side by the arms so that the foot of the Cross rests on</l><l xml:id="m-da4cbdcc-bd0b-4364-98aa-579908d238f6" facs="#m-adc11fbb-d0fc-4f70-9955-0c5fdd10d3d9" label="text-like">the steps.</l><l xml:id="m-2e78f9ee-14fe-4f1a-af45-98263e4285b2" facs="#m-7c30eb93-cc0d-4cfa-95e9-b31e85aebaa4" label="text-like">Meanwhile the two other acolytes lor serversl vho held the lighted candles</l><l xml:id="m-c327ad05-2dab-496c-9560-5983e877642c" facs="#m-aa6320c5-157f-4e08-bf77-77f0c9ce67b7" label="text-like">place them on each side of the Cross on the predella, and they hneel there on</l><l xml:id="m-c654b1ae-a016-4fb1-82ca-2cc4f6591733" facs="#m-1ffd709b-df34-409b-82cd-1c86bf5b7e25" label="text-like">each side of the predella facinɇ the Cross.</l><l xml:id="m-0c53ac3d-e753-4be5-afda-39e2f1bea046" facs="#m-b9ad8ced-8de0-48a2-8096-c825a53f3fc9" label="text-like">Having given the Cross to the acolytes Iserversl, the celebrant with the</l><l xml:id="m-d48a5258-52d5-4bf2-969a-5102d03cb998" facs="#m-5ef002c6-5c77-46df-b3eb-dfa0d8c00649" label="text-like">ministers Iservers), comes doun from the aliar, genufiects to the Cross, and</l><l xml:id="m-452d91c0-e485-4b8d-b30e-1d1ba5a8d642" facs="#m-52a05846-e16b-4ada-99db-69dfe4f4aaee" label="text-like">goes to the sedilia.</l><l xml:id="m-de2461a4-e1eb-443a-8de3-cb1b15aa54b5" facs="#m-fc103ce3-c1f8-49f0-b0a3-29bf7e24ade7" label="text-like">The adoration of the Cross then baeins as folloros: first the celebrant comes</l><l xml:id="m-4bc7d555-6602-4e60-ab92-f48d8a8e9e18" facs="#m-693c441c-e994-49fd-8e5d-efb2ffb37f79" label="text-like">alone, then the sacred ministers, then the clergy and lastly the servers. If it</l><l xml:id="m-18664b06-7c28-432c-b87f-6e5d822167d3" facs="#m-3aa53f5f-d265-4212-a504-4d776482117d" label="text-like">can be done conveniently, they all tate their shoes off, and they approach the</l><l xml:id="m-1467d80d-9922-4780-a5c7-0bd17a599400" facs="#m-bf02df27-40e8-417b-8009-849e27e55da1" label="text-like">Cross one after the other: after a simple genuflexion made three times, they</l><l xml:id="m-688fd269-c691-4a6d-b55f-2e2a3f578054" facs="#m-e201b4a8-302c-4ee6-b80f-27aff3ab338f" label="text-like">tiss the feet of the crucifix.</l><l xml:id="m-76a3b2a3-eaeb-4094-9e28-80e7a491684b" facs="#m-f1658a08-8832-4258-8252-eed90683e4ec" label="text-like">18. When the celebrant, ministers, clergy and servers have completed their</l><l xml:id="m-9e0bc1d7-ff79-4853-9cc8-04dc11c43901" facs="#m-e7de2b97-42ab-4700-a62a-1a954573a2be" label="text-like">adoration of the Cross, it is carried io the commumion-rail by the tuo acolvtes</l><l xml:id="m-6311bd71-f616-4acf-bdf2-e3a47c7feea3" facs="#m-a9a5ca39-7268-488a-a426-402549e30b10" label="text-like">Ior two serversl accompanied by the tuo other acolytes wiih lighted candles.</l><l xml:id="m-27d2c5b7-bf5f-4421-bfc5-c6efd562412e" facs="#m-38ff257b-bfcc-49b8-9b4b-e99e9e2f2836" label="lyrics-like">It is held therẽ in the same way as indicated above so that the faithful can</l><l xml:id="m-995eec6e-90d8-427e-9174-6c0314b27c6c" facs="#m-c1142d7d-e314-4661-94a1-1fe169b2bf72" label="text-like">come past the Cross as it were in procession, the men first and then the</l><l xml:id="m-67c0e19f-a97b-4c87-9721-bf4c91f66a15" facs="#m-91262d6e-fb2c-47ee-bac2-c4d77eec952d" label="text-like">uomen. They devouily hiss the feet of the crucifix after makine a simple</l><l xml:id="m-780c2ff4-98cc-424a-ae8d-4646c970d0e7" facs="#m-d328036f-b7ff-47ac-9e6d-f8ee4f110a27" label="ambiguous">gemglexion.</l><l xml:id="m-0a8f6f17-8427-4c0d-857e-8c03ce524f97" facs="#m-ac5c0629-2f72-47ed-9ca3-99185e0a848a" label="text-like">If the adoration of the Cross cannot be carried through without difficulty and</l><l xml:id="m-31db12b6-c8a0-48d0-b6af-5746bdf39f86" facs="#m-b997529f-32b2-4273-b80e-53e7c3079bd9" label="text-like">hindrance to good order and devotion, it moy be modified as follous: when</l><l xml:id="m-76c2e576-9b8d-4f9d-9688-7227f8d9d7e4" facs="#m-ec441780-f223-40d1-b624-7c3dc3dde65a" label="text-like">the clergy, or the servers, have finished their adoration the celebrant tahes</l><l xml:id="m-597385ae-4148-4eaa-a82d-f07c09dd3ad9" facs="#m-65806e55-fdc8-4c1f-bbc3-3e683c4a1ac4" label="text-like">the Cross from the servers; standing at the top of the altar steps, and firn</l><l xml:id="m-760b9560-2942-494f-bb7e-96a769fe3afe" facs="#m-4989d05f-56fa-46d4-a798-e4706ad7df6b" label="lyrics-like">briefty exhortins the people to adorẽ the holy Cross, he holds it up, offerins</l><l xml:id="m-eb96b473-2e71-4c90-b283-5eae4fc12e6c" facs="#m-d8134c57-4b75-479d-add5-a38a5526f8c9" label="text-like">it for their adoration, for a feto moments.</l><l xml:id="m-e6268e42-22dd-4cb8-a88f-a432ee6651b3" facs="#m-06ad3a40-7206-4901-b893-d6caf70d30b5" label="text-like">19. While the adoration of the Cross is tahins place, the schola (dividec</l><l xml:id="m-f780ddde-12bc-445a-980f-5355aeb5b34c" facs="#m-a44213f6-36e6-4258-ac15-40d9f898c8dc" label="text-like">into to choirsns the Reproaches and other chants, while the celebrant</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>